{{!-- The bar every Surface wears, in the three shapes the design draws.

Which shape a Surface gets is named at the call site, in the template, because the shape is a
property of the Surface and the Surface is the template — see the route map in DECISIONS.md.
It is not sniffed from the render context: a Surface's context depends on the buyer's
routes.yaml (this install's Feed reports `archive`, a bare install's reports `index`) and an
error page reports no context at all, so context is the one thing that cannot name a Surface.

	{{> "chrome/header"}}                 the listing bar: nav, search, Mode, Subscribe
	{{> "chrome/header" compact=true}}    the reading bar: shorter, no search control
	{{> "chrome/header" auth=true}}       the members bar: mark, a way back, Mode

Order inside the bar is fixed by the design: mark · nav · search · Mode · Subscribe · menu.

Search hands off to Ghost. The platform ships its own search — index, popup, keyboard — and
sodo-search binds to any element carrying `data-ghost-search`, so the design's ⌕ button is
that element and this theme writes no search code at all. Two measured details decide where
the attribute goes (sodo-search 1.8, `getCustomTriggerButtons`/`addKeyboardShortcuts`):

- the ⌘K shortcut is registered *only* if the page carries at least one trigger, so a
  Surface with no visible search control still needs one in its markup;
- the overlay below the nav breakpoint carries a trigger of its own, and it is in the DOM on
  every Surface even when the viewport is wide enough to hide it. That is what keeps ⌘K live
  on the reading bar, where the design draws no ⌕ at all.

The Mode switch renders once, here, on every shape. The reference build learned that the
hard way: a floating toggle placed per page turned into 22 copies. --}}
<header
	class="bg-surface border-border border-b"
	{{#unless auth}}x-data="siteMenu" x-on:resize.window="resized()"{{/unless}}>
	{{!-- The one control the design does not draw and every keyboard visitor needs. It has no
	pixels until it has focus, so it costs the reference nothing. --}}
	<a
		href="#main"
		class="btn btn-primary font-ui sr-only rounded-sm px-4 py-2 text-sm font-semibold no-underline focus:not-sr-only focus:absolute focus:top-2 focus:left-2 focus:z-50">{{t "Skip to content"}}</a>

	<div
		{{#unless auth}}x-ref="bar"{{/unless}}
		class="container flex flex-wrap items-center gap-y-4 {{#if auth}}gap-x-6 py-[18px]{{else}}gap-x-[30px] {{#if compact}}py-5{{else}}py-[22px]{{/if}}{{/if}}">

		{{#if auth}}
			{{> "chrome/wordmark" wrapper="mr-auto" logoHeight="h-4" titleSize="text-[22px]"}}

			<a
				href="{{@site.url}}"
				class="font-ui text-muted hover:text-accent text-sm no-underline"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> {{t "Back to site"}}</a>

			{{> "chrome/mode-toggle"}}
		{{else}}
			{{!-- Below the nav breakpoint the nav is gone, so the mark takes over pushing the
			remaining controls to the right edge. Both branches spell their classes out: a class
			assembled at render time is a class Tailwind's scanner never sees in the source. --}}
			{{#if compact}}
				{{> "chrome/wordmark" wrapper="max-nav:mr-auto" logoHeight="h-[17px]" titleSize="text-[24px]"}}
			{{else}}
				{{> "chrome/wordmark" wrapper="max-nav:mr-auto" logoHeight="h-[19px]" titleSize="text-[26px]"}}
			{{/if}}

			<nav
				aria-label="{{t "Main navigation"}}"
				class="nav:flex mr-auto hidden flex-wrap items-center gap-[22px]">{{navigation variant="bar"}}</nav>

			{{#unless compact}}
				<button
					type="button"
					aria-label="{{t "Search"}}"
					data-ghost-search
					class="btn border-border text-text hover:bg-surface-2 rounded-pill max-nav:hidden grid size-9 shrink-0 cursor-pointer place-items-center border bg-transparent font-mono text-sm">
					<span aria-hidden="true">⌕</span>
				</button>
			{{/unless}}

			{{> "chrome/mode-toggle"}}

			{{> "chrome/cta" class="btn btn-primary font-ui max-nav:hidden rounded-sm px-[18px] py-2.5 text-sm font-semibold no-underline"}}

			<button
				type="button"
				aria-label="{{t "Menu"}}"
				x-ref="burger"
				x-on:click="toggle()"
				x-bind:aria-expanded="menuOpen"
				aria-expanded="false"
				aria-controls="site-menu"
				class="btn border-border text-text hover:bg-surface-2 rounded-pill nav:hidden grid size-9 flex-none cursor-pointer place-items-center border bg-transparent">
				<span
					aria-hidden="true"
					class="flex size-9 flex-col items-center justify-center gap-[5px]">
					<span
						class="bg-text block h-[1.5px] w-4 transition-transform"
						x-bind:class="menuOpen ? 'translate-y-[3.25px] rotate-45' : ''"></span>
					<span
						class="bg-text block h-[1.5px] w-4 transition-transform"
						x-bind:class="menuOpen ? '-translate-y-[3.25px] -rotate-45' : ''"></span>
				</span>
			</button>
		{{/if}}
	</div>

	{{#unless auth}}
		{{> "chrome/menu"}}
	{{/unless}}
</header>
